{
  "_about": "laneHORSEBEHAV v1, read by Assets/Scripts/Mount/HorseBehaviour.cs (partial of AmbientHorses). enabled=false or this file missing = AmbientHorses exactly as before. rigMap swaps a breed glb for its rigged copy (the originals have no skeleton and no clips: 9 leg joints are skinned in by tools/make_rigs.py). gaits: the leg curves per speed (minMps = speed from which the gait is used, strideM = distance covered per full leg cycle, duty = share of the cycle a hoof is on the ground, liftM = hoof lift in the swing, offsets = leg phase FL FR HL HR; walk = lateral sequence, trot = diagonal pairs, gallop = transverse). Cycle rate = speed / strideM, so the planted hoof moves back exactly at the body speed. life: mode hits = hp / hitsToKill x weight per connecting swing (heavy swings count heavyWeight), mode damage = the move's own damage; respawnS is real time (UTC clock like the zone spawns), session only, nothing is written to a save. skit: the first hit sends the horse away from the attacker (startle, then gallop at fleeMps around props / arena / spot circles of every herd, inside its rectangle + boundsMarginM, stops after panicMinS..panicMaxS once fleeMinM away, stands calmPauseS, strolls again). roam: stroll targets stay edgeInsetM inside the herd rectangle and are pulled centerBias towards laneX. hit: capsule along the horse (halfLengthM, radiusM) judged with the Duel.Resolve reach / arc maths (+ assistArcDeg). target: soft lock (camera lock-on + marker + hp bar) on the nearest living horse in rangeM / coneDeg while Joan has no fight. Debug: command line -horsebehavdebug (or debugHitKey) = a virtual light hit on the targeted / nearest horse.",
